From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: benesjan <janbenes1234@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:31:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor!: rename L1->L2 message content/secret to
 public_content_hash/private_content

Labs side of the rename agreed in governance discussion #52. The Inbox data
model is unchanged; the fields are named for what they are: `content` is the
public content hash and `secret`/`secretHash` are the private content and its
hash.

- Aztec.nr: `consume_l1_to_l2_message(public_content_hash, private_content,
  sender, leaf_index)`, `compute_private_content_hash`,
  `DOM_SEP__PRIVATE_CONTENT_HASH`, TXE `send_l1_to_l2_message` (now takes the
  private content as an array) / `send_l1_to_l2_message_from_private_content_hash`.
  TXE oracle version bumped.
- Aztec.js / stdlib: `L1ToL2Message.{publicContentHash,privateContentHash}`,
  `computePrivateContentHash(privateContent: Fr[])`, `generateClaimSecret`
  removed.
- Bot: crosschain seeds and inbox bot records renamed; store schema bumped so
  older stores are discarded.
- CLI: `get-l1-to-l2-message-witness --private-content`.
- Contracts, e2e tests, docs and examples updated to the renamed L1 `Inbox` /
  `FeeJuicePortal` ABI.

